   "approvals": [],
   "design": "Radios with position reporting show crew and vehicle locations to dispatch, so the inspector relays positions only for crews off the network. The digital radio system logs the time and unit of each call, and the inspector adds the message summary. The positions and logs serve the incident record, not crew performance. Receiving and relaying messages, briefings and the danger board stay with the inspector.",
   "previous_blocker": "Positions were relayed by voice and calls logged by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Radios with position reporting and call logs.",
   "still_hard": "Valleys without radio coverage.",
   "human_edge": "Staying clear on the radio when a fire turns.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less relaying and logging; the emergency calls stay.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "dispatch",
     "task": "Track crews",
     "learn": "Whether positions are current."
    }
   ],
   "build_days": {
    "coding": "0",
    "integration": "1-2",
    "testing_rollout": "0-1",
    "consent_and_access": "0-1"
   },
   "run_cost": "low",
   "evidence": [
    {
     "claim": "Digital radio systems can report unit positions and log call times and units.",
     "grade": "E1",
     "source": "model knowledge",
     "kind": "capability"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Voice or location logs that show crew performance need works council consent.",
     "grade": "E1",
     "source": "[S8]",
     "kind": "legal"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Public bodies keep records in good, orderly and accessible state.",
     "grade": "E1",
     "source": "[S4]",
     "kind": "legal"
    }
   ],
   "assumptions": [
    "Boundary: relaying messages; maintaining records and logbooks (task 11108) is a sibling task, but the radio log is priced here because no answer for 11108 cuts it.",
    "s3 keeps 40 for crews on foot or out of coverage; s4 keeps 50 for the message summary.",
    "Using positions or call logs to judge crew performance would need works council consent; this design does not.",
    "Radio and phone are counted under mail and phone; the means prior counts them as in person (68%), a difference of convention."
   ],
   "unknowns": [
    "Radio coverage of the forest."
   ],
   "research_questions": [
